      "id": "format-time-value",
      "name": "FormatTimeValue",
      "category": "TimeUtils",
      "signature": "FormatTimeValue(Duration, Num Digits)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Duration",
          "type": "Double"
        },
        {
          "name": "Num Digits",
          "type": "Int",
          "default": "1"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "String",
      "docs": "double is a 64 bit IEEE 754 double precision Floating Point Number\n1 bit for the sign, 11 bits for the exponent, and 52* bits for the value\n15.5 decimal digits of precision (max value*: 4`503`599`627`370`495)\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| 900`000.000`000`001     --> up to 10 days   with    1 ns precision\n|  90`000.000`000`000`1   --> up to 25 hours  with  0.1 ns precision (100 ps)\n|   9`000.000`000`000`01  --> up to 2.5 hours with 0.01 ns precision (10 ps)\n|     900.000`000`000`001 --> up to 15 min    with    1 ps precision\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n|   3`600.000`000`000`001 --> 1 ps precision at 1 hour : NOT OK (16 digits)!!!\n|  86`400.000`000`000`001 --> 1 ps precision at 1 day  : NOT OK (17 digits)!!!\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
    },
